 ### Vessel Mask Extraction via Subtraction
-This variant isolates cerebral vasculature by computing the voxel-wise difference between a T1 contrast-enhanced dataset and a non-enhanced T1 dataset [S1]. The resulting difference image highlights contrast uptake, which watershed segmentation then converts into a binary vessel mask [S1]. It is selected when vascular structures must be visualized alongside anatomical details in volume rendering pipelines [S1].
+This variant isolates cerebral vasculature by computing the voxel-wise difference between a T1 contrast-enhanced dataset and a non-enhanced T1 dataset [S1]. The resulting difference image highlights contrast uptake, which watershed segmentation then converts into a binary vessel mask [S1]. It is selected when vascular structures must be visualized alongside anatomical details in volume rendering pipelines [S1]. It builds on [Region Growing Segmentation](9712-region-growing-segmentation.md) by using intensity subtraction rather than direct region merging.
 
